{"v":1,"built_at":"2026-10-29T08:47:49.568Z","core":{"appSha":"9f21d814e675","builtAt":"2026-10-29T02:52:33.177Z","schemaV":1},"key":"us/119-hr-1721","model":{"found":true,"billKey":"us/119-hr-1721","polity":"us","eyebrow":"United States","reference":"H.R. 1721","title":"Critical Infrastructure Manufacturing Feasibility Act","titleExpandable":false,"meta":"Commerce, Science, and Transportation Committee, Energy and Commerce Committee · Rep. Mariannette Miller-Meeks (R-IA)","summary":{"lead":"Official summary (Congressional Research Service, Introduced in House): ","blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Critical Infrastructure Manufacturing Feasibility Act","gap":"none"},{"kind":"para","text":"This bill requires the Department of Commerce to study and report on products that are in high demand across the critical infrastructure sectors. Critical infrastructure sectors are those whose assets, systems, and networks are vital to national security, the economy, public health or safety, or any combination of those matters.","gap":"para"},{"kind":"para","text":"The study must (1) identify the products in high demand across those sectors that are being imported due to manufacturing, material, or supply chain constraints; and (2) analyze the costs, benefits, and feasibility of manufacturing those products in the United States.","gap":"para"}]},"pathLabel":"The legislative path","latest":{"labelText":"Signed by Pres. Trump","glyph":{"icon":"scroll","badge":true},"date":"20 October 2026"},"asOf":{"lead":"Record as of ","date":"20 October 2026","note":"the most recent action in the official record. Status can lag; each step below carries its own date."},"groups":[{"spine":{"key":"rec-H.R. 1721-18","kind":"record","spine":true,"date":"20 October 2026","labelText":"Signed by Pres. Trump","glyph":{"icon":"scroll","badge":true},"postId":"us-20261021-fb7a5aff","postHref":"/p/us-20261021-fb7a5aff","whatsNext":{"lead":"What's next: ","text":"Takes effect (on enactment unless the text sets o